hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"401","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Bahili, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""What is sin?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: ""That which troubles your heart, so leave it."" He asked: ""What is faith?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: ""Whoever is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his bad deed, then he is a believer."
"402","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his bad deed, then he is a believer."
"403","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon at the place of Jabiyah, and he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us and he said... and he also mentioned this matter... and he narrated this hadith."
"404","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon at this very place of mine and said: “Honor my companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then falsehood will become apparent and such people will become widespread that each of them will give testimony though it will not be sought from him, and he will swear an oath though it will not be requested from him. So whoever likes the center of Paradise should adhere to the congregation, for indeed the devil is with the one who is alone and is farther from two. So no man should sit in seclusion with a woman, for the third among them is the devil. And whoever is grieved by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed, then he is a believer.”"
"405","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasted continuously, in reality, he did not fast."
"406","Note: The author has narrated this tradition with the chain of Imam ‘Aqili (may Allah have mercy on him). Imam ‘Aqili (may Allah have mercy on him) says: Muhammad bin Isma‘il narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim bin Qasim narrated to us, he was narrated by Abu ‘Aqili, he was narrated by Yazid bin Sinan, he says: I heard Bukayr bin Firoz, he said that I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever fears (danger in traveling late at night) sets out in the early part of the night, and whoever sets out in the early part of the night reaches his destination. Listen! Indeed, the merchandise of Allah is precious. Listen! The merchandise of Allah is Paradise.”"
"407","Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever desires the honor and greatness of the Hereafter should abandon the adornment of the world."
"408","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers many voluntary prayers at night, his face becomes very radiant during the day."
"409","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs many voluntary prayers at night, his face becomes very radiant during the day."
"410","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers many voluntary prayers at night, his face becomes very radiant during the day."
"411","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers many voluntary prayers at night, his face becomes very radiant during the day."
"412","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers many voluntary prayers at night, his face becomes very radiant during the day."" A large group of the Imams of Hadith have narrated this hadith, while Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali bin Umar al-Daraqutni selected and narrated this hadith from the narrations of Qadi Abu Tahir Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Dhahli, and no hadith scholar has pointed out any flaw in its chain or text. However, some Imams have rejected this hadith, saying that these (words are not actually a hadith but) are the words of Sharik bin Abdullah himself, and they have attributed the similarity found in these words to Thabit bin Musa al-Dhabi. Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ali al-Ghazi al-Mutawi, resident of Makkah, narrated to us ""by way of ijazah"" that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Hakim said: Qadi Sharik bin Abdullah was present in a hadith gathering, and the person who would dictate to the people after listening from him was in front of him. So Sharik read the chain of a hadith (and had only reached this point) and had not yet narrated the text of the hadith, when Thabit bin Musa entered the gathering. Upon seeing him, considering his asceticism and piety, Sharik said: ""Whoever offers many voluntary prayers at night, his face becomes very radiant during the day."" From this statement, Thabit bin Musa understood that the words Sharik had read with the chain were the text of the hadith, so based on his understanding, he would narrate these words as a hadith with Sharik's chain, although there is no basis for this hadith from that chain. And for this reason, some weak narrators, having stolen this hadith from Thabit bin Musa, narrated it from Qadi Sharik as a hadith. The reality is that this hadith is narrated through many chains, and also from many reliable narrators besides Thabit bin Musa and Qadi Sharik. Some of those chains are as follows."
"413","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers many voluntary prayers at night, his face is radiant during the day."
"414","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs many voluntary prayers at night, his face becomes very radiant during the day."
"415","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs many voluntary prayers at night, his face will be radiant during the day."
"416","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs many voluntary prayers at night, his face will be radiant during the day."
"417","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers many voluntary prayers at night, his face is radiant during the day."
"418","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves his worldly life harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves his Hereafter harms his worldly life. So give preference to that which is everlasting (the Hereafter) over that which is perishing (the world)."
"419","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever disgraces and humiliates Allah's ruler, Allah will disgrace and humiliate him, and whoever honors Allah's ruler, Allah will honor him."
"420","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever approves of the actions of a people, whether bad or good, is like those who do those actions."
"421","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever seeks refuge with you in the name of Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever asks you in the name of Allah, give to him; and whoever invites you, accept his invitation; and whoever does good to you, repay him; and if you do not find anything with which to repay him, then pray for him so much until you feel that you have repaid him.”"
"422","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “(A servant’s) richness is that he remains hopeless of what is in the hands of people, and whoever among you inclines towards any greed, he should proceed slowly.”"
"423","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever Allah has granted sixty years of age, then surely he has fulfilled the excuse regarding age.”"
"424","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever Allah has granted sixty years of age, then surely he has fulfilled the excuse regarding age."
"425","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith as marfu‘ to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “Whoever begins the morning without intending to wrong anyone, his sins are forgiven.”"
"426","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no sin in backbiting the one who has cast aside the cloak of modesty."
"427","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) has also narrated a similar report from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) through another chain of transmission... and narrated the hadith in the same manner."
"428","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is grieved by his mistake is forgiven, even if he does not seek forgiveness."
"429","Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever fears Allah, Allah will make everything fear him; and whoever does not fear Allah, Allah will make him fear everything.”"
"430","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever likes to meet Allah, Allah also likes to meet him, and whoever does not like to meet Allah, Allah also does not like to meet him."
"431","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever likes to meet Allah, Allah also likes to meet him, and whoever does not like to meet Allah, Allah also does not like to meet him."" Muslim has also narrated this with his chain in similar words."
"432","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever is asked about some knowledge which he knows, but he conceals it (and does not inform), a bridle of fire will be put on him."
"433","Qais bin Talq narrates from his father. And he (Qais's father) was among those who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) as part of a delegation. He says that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever is asked about some knowledge but conceals it, a bridle of fire will be put on him on the Day of Resurrection."
"434","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith of the cave, and at its end he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you can keep any of his good deeds hidden, he should do so."
"435","Hukm bin Umair (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""When a door of goodness is opened for someone, he should hasten to accept it, for he does not know when it may be closed to him."
"436","Dhamrah bin Habib, may Allah have mercy on him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When a door of goodness is opened for someone, he should hasten to accept it, for he does not know when it may be closed for him."
"437","One of the sons of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah narrated from his father, who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever suppresses his anger while being able to express it, Allah will fill him with security and faith. And whoever refrains from wearing beautiful clothes while being able to wear them—"" The narrator Bishr bin Mansur said: I think the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""—out of humility and modesty, Allah Almighty will clothe him with the garment of honor and dignity. And whoever arranges a marriage for the sake of Allah, Allah Almighty will crown him with the crown of kingship."
"438","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever walks towards the mosques in the darkness of the night, Allah Almighty will grant him light on the Day of Resurrection."
"439","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated it as marfu‘ that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever walks towards the mosques in the darkness of the night, Allah will grant him light on the Day of Resurrection."
"440","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to taste the sweetness of faith should love a person (and) love him only for the sake of Allah Almighty."" Yahya bin Salim is Abu Balj, and it has also been said that he is Ibn Abi Salim."
"441","It is narrated from Abu Salamah Hamsi that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever acquires wealth through unlawful means, Allah will lead him to destruction."
"442","It is narrated from Abu Salamah Hamsi that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever acquires wealth through unlawful means, Allah will lead him to destruction."
"443","Qarzi reports that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), Abu Sa‘id Khudri, and Mu‘awiyah (may Allah be pleased with them) gathered together. Mu‘awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever among you wishes, let him begin by narrating a hadith which he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), which his ears heard and his heart preserved. The two of them (Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah and Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id) said: You begin, narrate to us the hadith which you have remembered. He said: I will do so. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Guarantee me six things and I will guarantee you Paradise: When you speak, do not lie; when you make a promise, do not break it; when you are entrusted, do not betray; lower your gaze; guard your private parts; and restrain your hands (from oppression).” Then Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Abu Hurairah! Now you narrate. So he said: I heard Sayyiduna Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Three types of people will be presented before Allah with their hands tied to their necks: a ruler, a judge, and a chief. Only their justice will release them from this state, and whoever among them committed oppression will be in the most severe and deepest part of the Fire.” (Then) Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “The earth never trembles as much as it does due to the ritual bath after fornication or due to unjust killing. And whoever acquires wealth through unlawful means, Allah will cause it to be lost through the rights of people. And whoever goes to the worldly people in the morning or evening seeking the world, he may acquire it, but (in reality) he is among those who mock the signs of Allah. And whoever goes to a ruler and speaks contrary to the truth according to his desire, he will be his companion in the Fire. And whoever goes to a ruler and backbites his brother, Allah will make His mercy forbidden for him on the Day of Resurrection.” Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Mu‘awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) threw himself down from the couch. When the people left, he went to his sister, Umm al-Mu’minin Sayyidah Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her), and complained to her that Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them) had deliberately narrated to him such severe ahadith that he was deeply distressed. Sayyidah Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: By Allah! I have heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) even more than what Abu Hurairah mentioned. Mu‘awiyah asked: What is that? She said: “Whoever does a good deed, it is for him; and whoever does an evil deed, it is also for him.” Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: After the hadith you have narrated, who would desire rulership, judgment, or leadership (such positions)? She said: “The worst of Allah’s servants are those who say: O our Lord! Give us in this world, and for them there is nothing in the Hereafter.”"
"444","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever is given his share of gentleness has certainly been given his share of goodness in this world and the Hereafter, and whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has certainly been deprived of his share of goodness in this world and the Hereafter.”"
"445","Sayyida Umm al-Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from Sayyiduna Abu al-Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “Whoever is given his share of gentleness has indeed been given his share of goodness, and whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has indeed been deprived of his share of goodness.” And he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The heaviest thing in the scale of a believer is good character. Indeed, Allah Almighty hates the ill-mannered and foul-mouthed person.”"
"446","Qasim bin Muhammad (may Allah have mercy on him) says that I heard my paternal aunt, Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is granted his share of gentleness has been given his share of goodness in this world and the Hereafter."
"447","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever gives preference to the love of Allah over the love of people, Allah will suffice him from the hardships of people."
"448","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever separates himself from the congregation even by a handspan has removed the collar of Islam from his neck."
"449","Rabi’ (may Allah have mercy on him) says: When the (troublemaking) people set out towards Sayyiduna ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), I went to Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) in Mada’in. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever separates himself from the congregation and humiliates the leadership will meet Allah in such a state that he will have no status there.”"
"450","Zaid bin Aslam, may Allah have mercy on him, says that during the time of the Fitnah of Harrah, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, came to Ibn Muti’. He had a cushion brought for him and welcomed him. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: I have only come to you to tell you two things which I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. I heard him say: “Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience (to the Imam), he will have no proof or argument for himself on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever separates from the community dies the death of ignorance (Jahiliyyah).”"
"451","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said this statement at the place of Jabiyah in his sermon, narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to reside in the center of Paradise should adhere to the congregation, for the devil is with the lone person and is farther from two."
"452","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that at the place of Jabiyah, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon, and he mentioned a lengthy sermon, and in it was also this: ""Whoever among you desires the center of Paradise, then he should adhere to the congregation."" He mentioned it in a brief manner."
"453","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever returns the item sold by a remorseful person, Allah Almighty will overlook his slips on the Day of Resurrection."
"454","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever returns the item sold by a remorseful person, Allah Almighty will overlook his slips on the Day of Resurrection."
"455","Abu Ja'far (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever restrains his tongue from violating the honor of people, Allah Almighty will overlook his slips on the Day of Resurrection."
"456","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever separates a mother from her child, Allah will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"457","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever grows old in the state of Islam, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"458","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever makes things easy for a person in difficulty (regarding repayment of a debt), Allah will make things easy for him in this world and the Hereafter.”"
"459","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever grants respite to a person in difficulty or forgives him, Allah will shade him under His Throne on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade.”"
"460","Sayyiduna Abu al-Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever grants respite to a person in difficulty or forgives him, Allah will grant him His shade on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade.” The narrator says: Then Abu al-Yasar spat on his register (and erased the debtor’s name) and said to his debtor: Go, it is for you (i.e., your debt is forgiven), and the narrator mentioned that indeed the debtor was a person in difficulty."
"461","Sayyiduna Abu al-Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever grants respite to a person in difficulty or forgives him, Allah will grant him His shade on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade.”"
"462","‘Ubādah bin Walīd bin ‘Ubādah bin Ṣāmit (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates, and Walīd bin ‘Ubādah had the companionship of the Prophet (peace be upon him). (‘Ubādah) said: I went out with my father when I was a young boy. We met a man. (Walīd) said: Uncle! I have recognized you; you are among the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him). Thus, we gained the company of an elder. With this elder was his slave, who was carrying a register. My father said to him: Uncle! How did your morning go? He said: With well-being. My father said: I see signs of anger on your face. He said: Yes, so-and-so son of so-and-so owed a debt. I went in search of him. I greeted at his door, and a small child came out from the house. I asked him, and he said that he (the debtor) was at home. So I called out: O so-and-so! Come out to me. So he came out to me. I said: What made you delay when I greeted you, but you neither came out nor replied to me? He said: By the One besides whom there is no deity, I had nothing (money), and indeed I feared that I would lie to you or make a promise and then break it. I said: Is it really by Allah, besides whom there is no deity? He said: Yes, by Allah, besides whom there is no deity. (Abū al-Yasar) said: I bear witness to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him); my ears heard him say and my heart retained it: “Whoever gives respite to a debtor in difficulty or forgives him, Allah will shade him on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade.” He said: Therefore, I erased that document from him. ‘Ubādah bin Walīd says: He (Abū al-Yasar) was wearing a striped cloak and an embroidered mantle, and his slave was also wearing similar clothing. He says: I said: Uncle! What prevented you from giving this embroidered mantle to your slave and taking the striped cloak from him, so that you would have two striped cloaks and he would have two embroidered mantles? He says: He turned to me and said (to my father): Is this your son? He said: Yes. So he passed his hand over my head and said: May Allah bless you. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: “Feed them (your slaves) with what you eat and clothe them with what you wear.” My nephew! The loss of worldly goods is dearer to me than that the Hereafter’s goods be taken from me. I said to my father: Abūji! Who is this elder? He said: This is Abū al-Yasar bin ‘Amr."
"463","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is two-tongued in this world, two tongues of fire will be made for him on the Day of Resurrection."" Ibn Khayr (may Allah have mercy on him) said regarding this hadith: «اللہ تعالیٰ قیامت کے دن اس کے لیے آگ کی دو زبانیں بنائے گا۔»"
"464","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever looks into his brother's book (or writing) without his permission, it is as if he is looking into the fire."
"465","Sayyiduna Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever commands someone to do a good deed, his own conduct should also be good."
"466","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes forty mornings purely for Allah, streams of wisdom will flow from his heart onto his tongue."" It is as if the Prophet (peace be upon him) meant the person who attends the congregational prayer of Isha and Fajr for forty days. ""And whoever attains these two prayers with the first takbir for forty days, for him there are two salvations: for a man, there are two salvations, one salvation from the Fire and one salvation from hypocrisy."
"467","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."
"468","Sayyiduna Abu Shurayh Khuzai (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should treat his neighbor well, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.”"
"469","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."
"470","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor."
"471","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Shurayh Khuza'i, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. His hospitality is for one day and one night, and guest hospitality is for three days; after that, whatever is given is charity. And it is not permissible for any (guest) to stay with his host to the extent that he becomes a burden and hardship for him."
"472","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “For the person at whose hand someone accepts Islam, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.”"
"473","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever helps his brother in his absence, Allah Almighty will help him in this world and the Hereafter.”"
"474","Abu al-Hasan Ali bin Umar al-Daraqutni, may Allah have mercy on him, said in ""Kitab al-‘Ilal"" that Humaid al-Tawil narrated from Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said and... he narrated this hadith... did."
"475","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever helps his brother in his absence while he has the ability to help him, Allah Almighty will help him in this world and the Hereafter.”"
"476","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever relieves his brother from any of the worldly troubles, Allah will relieve him from any of the troubles of the Day of Resurrection. And whoever conceals the faults of his brother, Allah will conceal his faults in this world and the Hereafter. And Allah remains in the help of His servant as long as the servant is in the help of his brother."" The narrator, Ali bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him), said: I have received this information that by ""rajul"" is meant A‘mash (from whom Muhammad bin Wasi‘ narrated)."
"477","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not oppress him nor does he let him be oppressed, and whoever fulfills the need of his brother, Allah fulfills his need."
"478","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever remains engaged in fulfilling the need of his believing brother, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, remains engaged in fulfilling his need."
"479","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even if it is as small as a bird’s nest, a house will be built for him in Paradise."" Or he said: ""Allah will build his house in Paradise."
"480","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even if it is as small as a bird’s nest, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"481","Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever seeks knowledge and attains it, a double reward is written for him, and whoever seeks knowledge but is unable to attain it, a single reward is written for him.”"
"482","Amr bin Murrah, may Allah have mercy on him, says that we were sitting with Abu Ubaidah when people started discussing ostentation. An elder whose kunya was Abu Yazid said: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, say that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Whoever shows his deeds to people, Allah will make that deed reach the ears of His creation on the Day of Resurrection and will humiliate and disgrace him."
"483","Amr bin Murrah (may Allah have mercy on him) says that a person narrated a hadith to us in the house of Abu Ubaidah, that he heard Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrate a hadith from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and... he narrated this hadith, but it did not contain the words «يوم القيامة» (on the Day of Resurrection)."
"484","Sayyiduna Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks worldly gain in exchange for work meant for the Hereafter, he will have no share in the Hereafter."
"485","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever has a favor done to him and he gives nothing in return except praise of his benefactor, then surely he has expressed gratitude to him. And whoever conceals (the benefactor’s favor), then surely he has shown ingratitude.”"
"486","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a favor done to him should repay it, and whoever is not able to do so should praise (the benefactor), and whoever does not do so has certainly shown ingratitude."
"487","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is treated with kindness should repay it; if he is unable to do so, then he should mention (the kindness or the benefactor). If he mentions it, then indeed he has expressed gratitude for it. And whoever pretends and displays something which he does not possess, he is like one who wears a garment of falsehood."" And in the narration of Malini and Ibn Kharras (may Allah have mercy on them) the words are: «بما لم ينل» (with something which he has not attained)."
"488","Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does a good deed to any individual from Banu Abd al-Muttalib in this world, and he (the recipient) is unable to repay him in this world, then on the Day of Resurrection I will repay him on his behalf."
"489","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever sees a fault (in a Muslim) and then conceals it, it is as if he has brought a buried-alive girl out of her grave and given her life."
"490","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him), he says that it was said to him: Some of our neighbors drink alcohol, should we seize them and hand them over (to the police)? He said: No, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever sees a fault (in a Muslim) and then conceals it... al-hadith."
"491","Abu Dawood (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Muslim bin Ibrahim narrated to us with his chain the like of this, and he did not say the words «من قبرها» (from his grave)."
"492","Ali bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Muslim bin Ibrahim narrated to us with his chain the like of it, and he did not say the words «من قبرها» (from his grave)."
"493","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever turns completely towards Allah, Allah will suffice him in every difficulty and will provide for him from where he does not even imagine. And whoever turns away from Allah towards the world, Allah will leave him to that (world)."
"494","This narration is also reported through another chain from Fudayl bin ‘Iyad (may Allah have mercy on him) in a similar manner, and in it he has mentioned the words «كفاه الله مونته» (Allah will suffice him in his difficulty)."
"495","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever turns completely towards Allah, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will suffice him in his difficulty and will provide for him from where he does not even expect. And whoever turns away from Allah and inclines towards the world, Allah will hand him over to that (world)."
"496","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"497","This narration is also reported through another chain from Fudayl bin ‘Iyad, may Allah have mercy on him, in a similar manner."
"498","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks praise from people through acts of disobedience to Allah, the one who praises him will eventually become his critic."
"499","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks the pleasure of Allah by displeasing the people, Allah will be pleased with him and will make the people pleased with him as well. And whoever seeks the pleasure of the people by displeasing Allah, Allah will be displeased with him and will make the people displeased with him as well."
"500","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks the pleasure of Allah by displeasing the people, Allah will be pleased with him and will make the people pleased with him as well. And whoever seeks the pleasure of the people by displeasing Allah, Allah will be displeased with him and will make the people displeased with him as well."
"501","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever pleases Allah by displeasing the people, Allah will suffice him, and whoever pleases the people by displeasing Allah, Allah will entrust him to the people."
"502","Abu Abdur Rahman Hubli and Khalid bin Abi Imran (may Allah have mercy on them) report that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have good hope for the one who dies upon his good deeds, and be apprehensive about the one who dies upon his bad deeds, but do not despair."
"503","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""If a person commits a sin in this world and then receives its punishment, it is far from Allah's justice that He would punish His servant for that sin again. And if a person commits a sin and Allah conceals it in this world and pardons him, then it is far from Allah's greatness that He would punish him again for a sin He has already pardoned."
"504","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not possess that taqwa (God-consciousness) which can prevent him from disobeying Allah in solitude, then Allah does not care about anything else from his (other) deeds."
"505","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs his prayer well when people are watching him, then performs it badly when he is alone, this is mockery. With this, he has mocked his Lord."
"506","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs his prayer well when people are watching him, and performs it badly when he is alone, this is mockery. With this, he has mocked his Lord."
"507","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs prayer well when people are watching him, and performs it badly when he is alone, then this is mockery. With this, he has mocked his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."
"508","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a person's prayer does not prevent him from indecency and sin, (then understand that) it has only distanced him further from Allah."
"509","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever's prayer does not prevent him from indecency and sin, (then know that) through it he only becomes further from Allah."
"510","Abu Abdur Rahman Salami (may Allah have mercy on him) says that I heard Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) saying on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has any good or bad deed hidden, Allah manifests a sign of it upon him by which he is recognized."" And (in this chain) there is no mention of Sa'd bin Ubaidah between Alqamah bin Murshid and Abu Abdur Rahman."
"511","Abu Abdur Rahman Salami (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: I heard him say on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a person's good or bad deed is hidden, Allah manifests a sign of it upon him by which he is recognized."
"512","Al-Zuhri, may Allah have mercy on him, says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever seeks to accomplish something through sin will never have his hope fulfilled; rather, he will come very close to that which he was trying to avoid."
"513","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever tries to accomplish his task through sin will never have his hope fulfilled; rather, he will come very close to that which he was trying to avoid."
"514","Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she swore an oath regarding one of her slaves who had asked her for freedom, that Allah would never free him from Hell if she set him free. Then, for as long as Allah willed, she remained firm on her oath. Then she said: Subhan Allah! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever swears an oath to do or not do something, then sees a better option, should offer expiation for his oath and then choose the better option."
"515","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath regarding doing or not doing something, then sees a better option, he should offer expiation for his oath and choose the better option."
"516","Abdur Rahman bin Udhainah, may Allah have mercy on him, narrates from his father that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever swears an oath regarding something and then sees a better alternative, he should choose the better alternative and offer expiation for his oath."
"517","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever swears an oath regarding something and then sees a better option, he should offer expiation for his oath and choose the better option."
"518","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that a man asked Sayyiduna Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) for something, so he swore that he would not give it to him. Then he said: If I had not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever swears an oath about something, then sees something better than it, let him offer expiation for his oath and do that which is better,"" I would never have given it to you. Then he gave it to him."
"519","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath regarding something, then sees a better alternative than it, he should offer expiation for his oath and choose the better alternative."
"520","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any one of you swears an oath regarding something, then sees a better alternative, he should pay the expiation for his oath and choose what is better."
"521","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Samurah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""When you swear an oath about something, then offer the expiation for your oath and choose the action which is better."
"522","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is tested with these daughters and then treats them well, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."
"523","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that a woman came to me in such a state that her two daughters were with her, and she was asking (for something). I could not find anything with me except one date, so I gave her the date. She divided it into two parts and gave them to her two daughters, and she herself did not eat anything from it. Then she got up and left. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came, so I told him about this. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is tested concerning these daughters, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."
"524","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a bird without reason, then on the Day of Resurrection that (bird) will come in such a state that it will be crying out near the Throne, saying: O my Lord! Ask him why he killed me."
"525","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever asks people for their wealth in order to increase his own wealth, in reality he is asking for a burning coal. Now it is up to him, he may ask for a little or he may ask for more."" Muslim narrated it from Abu Kurayb and Wasl bin Abdul A'la (may Allah have mercy on them), they said that Ibn Fudayl (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us with his chain, and he narrated the like of it."
"526","Sayyiduna Ziyad bin Harith Suda'i رضي الله عنه reports that a man came to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and asked him about charity. The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Whoever asks despite being well-off, it will be a cause of headache and stomach illness for him."
"527","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to a food invitation while he was not invited to it, then indeed he enters as a thief and leaves as a bandit."
"528","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is invited but does not accept the invitation has indeed disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, and whoever attends an invitation without being invited enters as a thief and leaves as a bandit."
"529","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters someone's house without their permission, he enters as a thief and comes out as a robber."
"530","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intercedes with a ruler for his Muslim brother in a good deed or in resolving a difficulty, Allah will help him to cross the Bridge (Sirat) on the Day when feet will slip."
"531","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intercedes with a ruler on behalf of his Muslim brother in a good deed or in resolving a difficulty, Allah will help him cross the Bridge (Sirat) on the Day of Judgment at the time when feet will slip."
"532","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intercedes with a ruler for his Muslim brother in a good deed or in resolving a difficulty, Allah will help him cross the Bridge of Sirat on the Day of Judgment at the time when feet will slip."
"533","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats the pieces of food that have fallen from the dining mat, he, his children, and the children of his children will be protected from leukoderma, leprosy, and insanity."
"534","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever plays Nardashir (backgammon) is like one who has soiled his hand with the flesh and blood of a pig."
"535","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever plays Nardashir (backgammon) is like the one who has soiled his hand with the flesh of a pig."" Muslim ibn Hajjaj narrated it through the chain of Zuhair ibn Harb from Abdur Rahman ibn Mahdi from Sufyan (may Allah have mercy on them), and in it he said: «فكانما صبغ يده» (So it is as if he has soiled his hand)."
"536","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever becomes a guest of a people should by no means keep a voluntary fast without their permission."
"537","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever shuns an innovator, Allah will fill his heart with peace and faith, and whoever humiliates an innovator, Allah will grant him safety on the Day of Great Terror (the Day of Judgment), and whoever shows leniency towards him, honors him, or meets him with a cheerful face, then surely he has belittled the Shari’ah that was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).”"
"538","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever humiliates an innovator, Allah will grant him security on the Day of Great Dread."
"539","Sayyida Umm al-Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from Sayyiduna Abu al-Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever wakes up in the morning in a state of physical health, feeling secure regarding himself, and has the food for his day, then it is as if the whole world has been gathered and given to him.”"
"540","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Muhsin (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you wakes up in the morning feeling secure in his property, healthy in his body, and has food for one day, it is as if the whole world has been gathered for him."
"541","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever instills the love of the world in his heart will certainly be afflicted with three things: such toil whose fatigue will never end, such greed that will never lead to wealth, and such hope that will never reach its objective."
"542","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is made responsible for any matter concerning the Muslims, and Allah intends good for him, He provides him with a righteous minister who reminds him when he forgets and helps him when he remembers. And among the Muslims, there is no one with a greater reward than a righteous minister who, while being with a ruler, obeys him and also commands him with the commands of Allah, the Exalted."
"543","Sayyiduna Husayn bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that my father, Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is appointed as a leader over the people and then does not oppress them, does not lie to them when speaking, and does not break his promise when he makes one, then such a person is among those whose dignity is complete, whose justice is manifest, whose brotherhood is obligatory, and whose backbiting is forbidden."
"544","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “Whoever is afflicted by hunger and then presents it before people, his hunger will never be removed; but if he presents it before Allah, soon Allah will make him self-sufficient—either he will soon receive some wealth or he will soon become self-sufficient.”"
"545","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I and Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) were with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when he said: ""Whoever safeguards that which is between his two jaws and that which is between his two legs will enter Paradise."
"546","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guarantees me what is between his two jaws (the tongue) and what is between his two legs (the private parts), I guarantee him Paradise."" Imam Tabarani (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Only Ma'qil bin Ubaidullah has narrated it from Amr bin Dinar, and among those who narrated from him, Mughira is unique."
"547","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, then he should make his abode in the Hellfire."
"548","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Indeed, what prevents me from narrating more hadiths to you is that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, then he should make his abode in the Hellfire."
"549","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that I said to (my father) Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him): Indeed, I do not hear as many hadiths from you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) as so-and-so and so-and-so narrate. He said: I was never separated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), but I heard him say: ""Whoever attributes a lie to me, then he should make his abode in the Hellfire."
"550","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You may name yourselves after my name, but do not take my kunyah... (the hadith continues). And in the same hadith: 'And whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, then he should prepare his abode in the Hellfire.'"
"551","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, then he should prepare his abode in the Hellfire."
"552","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, then he should make his abode in the Hellfire."
"553","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... A similar hadith has been narrated. Musa (may Allah have mercy on him) said: We have heard this hadith only from Abdula'la, and Abu Awanah narrates this hadith from Abdula'la, from Sa'id bin Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, through this chain of narration."
"554","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware regarding narrating hadith from me, for whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me should make his abode in the Hellfire, and whoever lies about the Qur'an without knowledge should also make his abode in the Hellfire."
"555","Abu Maryam (may Allah have mercy on him) says that I heard Sayyiduna Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) saying to Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him): ""I ask you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his place in Hell'?"" So Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and did not say anything."
"556","Sayyiduna Rafi‘ bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever deliberately fabricates a lie against me, then he should make his abode in Hell.”"
"557","Sayyiduna Ya'la bin Murrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever deliberately attributes even a small lie to me, then he should make his abode in Hell."
"558","Sayyiduna Aws bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fabricates a lie against his Prophet, or his brothers, or his parents, will not even smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"559","Sayyiduna Amr bin Ubah رضي الله عنه narrates from the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم that he صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, then he should make his abode in Hell."
"560","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me in order to mislead people, then he should make his abode in Hell."
"561","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Surely, you will be helped, and you will be granted victory, and you will receive spoils of war. So whoever reaches that (time), he should fear Allah, enjoin good, and forbid evil. And whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, then he should prepare his abode in Hell."
"562","Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him prepare his abode in the Hellfire."
"563","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him make his abode in the Hellfire."
"564","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him prepare his abode in the Hellfire.”"
"565","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him prepare his abode in the Hellfire.”"
"566","Sayyiduna Nabit bin Shurit (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him prepare his abode in the Hellfire."
"567","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Paradise has been veiled with hardships and difficulties, and Hell has been veiled with carnal desires."" Ishaq al-Farawi, may Allah have mercy on him, is unique in narrating this."
"568","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hell has been veiled with carnal desires, and Paradise has been veiled with hardships and difficulties."" Imam Muslim (may Allah have mercy on him) has also narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) with his chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated the hadith."
"569","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The love of Allah becomes obligatory for the person who is angered but acts with patience."
"570","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent with concise speech and I have been supported with awe."
"571","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said... and he narrated this hadith."
"572","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I was helped by the east wind (Saba), and the people of ‘Ad were destroyed by the west wind (Dabur).”"
"573","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was helped by the east wind (Saba), and the people of ‘Ad were destroyed by the west wind (Dabur)."
"574","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"575","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was helped by the east wind (Saba), and the people of ‘Ad were destroyed by the west wind (Dabur)."" Imam Tabarani (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Only Abu ‘Awanah narrated it from Qatadah, and Muhammad bin Aban is unique in narrating it from him."
"576","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your Lord likes the youth who has no greed or desire."
"577","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""As you are, so will be those set in authority over you."" Or (he said): ""So will be the leaders appointed over you."
"578","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, people will be raised according to their intentions."
"579","Ali bin Musa (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his father, who narrates from his forefathers with a connected chain of transmission, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who gives false testimony will be raised on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he will be licking his tongue in the Fire just as a dog licks with its tongue in filth."
"580","Mus'ab bin Sa'd (may Allah have mercy on him) says that Sayyiduna 'Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by some people who were practicing archery. He pointed out their weakness, so they said: ""O Commander of the Faithful! We are just learning."" He said: ""The word you have spoken is harsher to us than your poor aim. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'May Allah have mercy on the person who corrects his tongue.'"
"581","It is narrated from Hasan al-Basri, may Allah have mercy on him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""May Allah have mercy on the servant who, when he speaks, earns a reward, or when he remains silent, stays in safety."
"582","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said three times: “May Allah have mercy on the person who, when he speaks, earns a reward, or when he remains silent, stays safe.”"
"583","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us several times and said: “May Allah have mercy on those who use a toothpick during ablution and after eating.”"
"584","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who narrates from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: ""Whoever is kept busy with My remembrance from asking Me, I will give him better than what I give to those who ask."
"585","Ja'far bin Muhammad, may Allah have mercy on him, narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, who said that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, Umar, and Abu Ubaidah, may Allah be pleased with them, gathered together and were discussing something. Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to them: ""Come with us to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."" So when they presented themselves before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, they said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We have come to you to ask about something."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If you wish, you may ask, and if you wish, I will myself tell you what you have come for."" Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to them: ""You have come to ask me about sustenance—where does it come from and how does it come? (Listen) Allah has decreed that He will surely provide sustenance to His believing servant from such a place where he would not even imagine."" This hadith is brief."
"586","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is near that poverty and neediness may reach to disbelief, and it is near that envy may overcome destiny."
"587","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"588","Ja'far bin Muhammad, may Allah have mercy on him, narrates from his father who said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever recognizes the people has been singled out for trial, and whoever does not recognize them will live among them."
"589","Mus'ab bin Sa'd (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his father, who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer may have any trait by nature, but not treachery and not lying."
"590","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""A believer's nature can have every trait except treachery and lying."
"591","Mus'ab bin Sa'd (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his father, who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer may have any trait by nature except treachery and lying."
"592","Hukm bin Umair (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You build such buildings in which you cannot live, and you accumulate wealth which you cannot consume."" And he narrated this hadith in a concise manner."
"593","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while advising us said: ""O human, whose end is death; O human, whose destination is the grave; O human, whose clothing is the shroud; O human, whose pillow is the dust; O human, whose neighbors are insects and worms; O human, whose visitors are Munkar and Nakir; O human, who will soon leave his wife; how many are there who welcome today but will not complete it, and how many are there who await tomorrow but will not reach it. If you were to see death and its swiftness, you would surely begin to dislike hopes and their deceptions."
"594","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am amazed at the heedless one, though heedlessness is not shown towards him; I am amazed at the one who longs for the world, though death is in search of him; and I am amazed at the one who laughs out loud, though he does not know whether he has pleased Allah or angered Him."
"595","Abu Ja'far Abdullah bin Masur Hashimi, may Allah have mercy on him, says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""How astonishing is the person who doubts Allah's power while he observes his own creation; how astonishing is the person who denies resurrection while he witnesses the first creation (of himself); how astonishing is the person who denies being brought back to life after death while every day and every night he dies and is brought back to life; how astonishing is the person who affirms the eternal abode yet strives for the abode of deception; and how astonishing is the person who is arrogant and boastful, while in reality he was created from a drop of fluid, then will become a decayed corpse, and in that state he does not know what will be done with him."
"596","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How amazing is the believer! By Allah, whatever Allah decides for the believer is always better for him."
"597","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Day of Judgment has drawn near, and people are increasing in their greed for the world, and their distance (from Allah) is only increasing."
"598","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam grows old, but two things in him remain young: the desire for wealth and the desire for a long life."" Imam Muslim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated it from Yahya bin Yahya, Sa'id bin Mansur, and Qutaybah bin Sa'id, and all of them narrated from Abu 'Awanah (may Allah have mercy on him) with a similar narration."
"599","Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman Quraishi (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that I was present with A’mash (may Allah have mercy on him) when someone said to him: Hasan bin ‘Ammarah (the governor) commits oppression. So he said: It is astonishing that an oppressive person is appointed to oppressive tasks; what else can be expected from an arrogant and oppressive person? Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman says that after this I went to Hasan bin ‘Ammarah and mentioned this to him. He sent a handkerchief and some clothes through a man as a gift to A’mash. The next day I went to A’mash a little early, thinking that before people arrived, I would speak to him. I again brought up the mention of Hasan bin ‘Ammarah, so A’mash said: Wonderful, wonderful, what can be said about Hasan bin ‘Ammarah? How many good deeds he does! So I said: Is this not the same person about whom you spoke yesterday? And today you are praising him, what is this? He replied: Leave these matters. Khaythamah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to me from Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “It is natural that the heart inclines towards the one who does good, and the heart feels aversion towards the one who does evil.”"
"600","Ismail bin Khayyat (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Hasan bin Ammarah came to know that A’mash had made some inappropriate remarks about him, so Hasan bin Ammarah sent him some clothes. After that, A’mash adopted a praiseworthy attitude towards Hasan bin Ammarah. When he was asked about this change, that previously you used to criticize him and now you are praising him, he replied: Khaythamah narrated to me from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, it is a natural matter that hearts...” Ibn ‘Adi says: I have written this hadith as marfu’ only from this teacher; otherwise, this hadith is known from A’mash as mawquf."
